      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "43f498f6-9afb-5426-b86a-d0e674d66fcd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arturo Beltrán Leyva, Héctor Beltrán Leyva, Edgar Valdez Villarreal\n- Organizations: Beltrán Leyva Cartel\n- Events: Arturo Beltrán Leyva's death, cartel faction conflict\n\nFacts:\n- In December 2009, the Mexican military killed Arturo Beltrán Leyva, the top boss of the Beltrán Leyva Cartel.\n- After Arturo Beltrán Leyva's death, Héctor Beltrán Leyva took control of one faction of the Beltrán Leyva Cartel.\n- After taking control of that faction, Héctor Beltrán Leyva declared war on Edgar Valdez Villarreal.\n- Before December 2009, Edgar Valdez Villarreal had long served as Arturo Beltrán Leyva's right hand.\n- Edgar Valdez Villarreal was born on August 11, 1973.\n- Edgar Valdez Villarreal, also known as La Barbie, is a Mexican American suspected drug lord and a leader of the Beltrán Leyva Cartel, a criminal group based in Sinaloa.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
